# Files owned by the user — fern generate will not overwrite these.
#
# `custom.rs` must live in the directory the generated `[[bin]]` builds from,
# because generated `main.rs` reaches it via `mod custom;`. When the generator
# renames that directory, this path has to move with it — otherwise the file
# survives regeneration while silently dropping out of the build. That is exactly
# what happened on 2026-08-05: this entry still read `cli/athena/custom.rs`, the
# file was duly preserved, and the binary moved to `cli/athena-intelligence-api/`
# and compiled against the generator's 1.6 KB stub instead. It still compiled, so
# nothing failed — the custom commands just stopped existing.
cli/athena-intelligence-api/custom.rs

# CI is never generated. Without this the whole directory is wiped on every
# regeneration — including build-cli.yml, the workflow that builds and releases
# the binaries, and the only thing that would have caught the loss above.
.github/

# README.md is generator-emitted (a template — the one that shipped literal
# `<org>/<repo>` placeholders for two months). It is hand-written now: install
# instructions, the truncation warning, the env-var migration note, the release
# process. Without this entry every regeneration reverts it to the template;
# regeneration PR #16 demonstrated exactly that by stripping the hand-added
# learning-guide link.
README.md

# Hand-written operator guide. The generator owns the docs/ directory and
# deletes files there it did not emit — regeneration PR #16 deleted this exact
# file two regenerations after it was merged in #15.
docs/athena-cli-learning.md

# The installer published at raw.githubusercontent.com/.../main/install.sh and
# consumed by every release's install instructions. Never generated. Root-level
# unknown files have so far survived regeneration (dist-workspace.toml did),
# but "so far survived" is not a contract — the learning guide above is what
# relying on that looks like.
install.sh

# Deleted, and the generator must not bring it back. The CLI generator's
# template emits this cargo-dist config, but nothing in this repo invokes
# cargo-dist — releases are cut by .github/workflows/release.yml, which does the
# same job explicitly (and still builds with [profile.dist] from Cargo.toml).
# It was removed in PR #18 and the very next regeneration (PR #19, both in the
# archived pre-2026-09-02 repository) re-created it from
# the template; this entry is what makes the removal stick.
dist-workspace.toml
